   "name": "Who moved in with his auntie and uncle in Bel-Air?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Will Smith is a fictionalized West Philadelphia teenager sent to live with rich relatives in The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air (1990), played by Will Smith. The character turned a rapper into a television and film superstar."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who dances to Tom Jones in The Fresh Prince?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Carlton Banks is Will's preppy, overachieving cousin in The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air (1990), played by Alfonso Ribeiro. His joyful dance to It's Not Unusual, the Carlton, became a permanent pop culture moment."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who was the dad in The Cosby Show?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Dr. Cliff Huxtable is a Brooklyn obstetrician raising five children with his lawyer wife in The Cosby Show (1984), played by Bill Cosby. The series topped ratings and reshaped images of Black family life."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who was the mom and lawyer in The Cosby Show?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Clair Huxtable is an elegant, sharp-witted attorney and mother of five in The Cosby Show (1984), played by Phylicia Rashad. She became a lasting model of Black professional womanhood and motherhood on television."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who wore flip-up glasses in A Different World?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Dwayne Wayne is a math whiz from Brooklyn at Hillman College, a fictional HBCU, in A Different World (1987), played by Kadeem Hardison. His flip-up glasses and romance with Whitley defined the series."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the Southern belle in A Different World?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Whitley Gilbert is a pampered Southern belle who grows into a thoughtful art student at Hillman College in A Different World (1987), played by Jasmine Guy. Her drawling delivery made her the show's breakout star."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who asked if he did that in Family Matters?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Steve Urkel is the accident-prone, suspender-wearing nerd next door in Family Matters (1989), played by Jaleel White. Meant as a one-time guest, his Did I do that catchphrase took over the show."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who does Steve Urkel have a crush on in Family Matters?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Laura Winslow is the smart, popular daughter of the Winslow family and the object of Steve Urkel's devotion in Family Matters (1989), played by Kellie Shanygne Williams across all nine seasons."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the Detroit radio and TV host in Martin?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Martin Payne is a loud, lovable Detroit broadcaster juggling work, friends and his girlfriend Gina in Martin (1992), played by Martin Lawrence, who also played many other characters in wild costumes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who runs Flavor magazine in Living Single?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Khadijah James is a Brooklyn magazine editor sharing a brownstone with friends in Living Single (1993), played by Queen Latifah. The series celebrated young Black women's careers and friendships before Friends made the format famous."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the attorney at law in Living Single?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Maxine Shaw is a razor-tongued attorney, Khadijah's roommate and Kyle's sparring partner turned love interest, in Living Single (1993), played by Erika Alexander. Her introductions of herself became a fan-favorite running joke."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who keeps a diary in Moesha?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Moesha Mitchell is a Los Angeles teenager writing her way through school, family and first love in Moesha (1996), played by singer Brandy. The series was a flagship of UPN and a defining 90s teen sitcom."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the studious twin in Sister, Sister?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Tia Landry is the serious, studious twin separated at birth and reunited as a teenager in Sister, Sister (1994), played by Tia Mowry opposite her real twin Tamera, a favorite of family audiences."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who has visions in That's So Raven?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Raven Baxter is a San Francisco teenager who can see glimpses of the future and disguises herself to change them in That's So Raven (2003), played by Raven-Symon\u00e9 in Disney Channel's landmark hit series."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who narrates his own childhood in Everybody Hates Chris?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Chris is a fictionalized teenage Chris Rock growing up in 1980s Brooklyn, bused to a mostly white school, in Everybody Hates Chris (2005), played by Tyler James Williams with narration by the real Chris Rock."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who robs drug dealers in The Wire?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Omar Little is a Baltimore stick-up man who only robs drug dealers, follows his own code, and terrifies the street when he whistles in The Wire (2002), played by Michael K. Williams in a career-defining role."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who ran the Barksdale organization in The Wire?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Russell Stringer Bell is the business-minded second-in-command of Baltimore's Barksdale drug organization, taking economics classes to go legitimate, in The Wire (2002), played by Idris Elba in his American breakout role."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the lawyer at the center of Girlfriends?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Joan Clayton is a successful Los Angeles attorney whose close circle of friends anchors Girlfriends (2000), played by Tracee Ellis Ross. The series ran eight seasons chronicling Black women's work, love and friendship."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is J.D.'s best friend in Scrubs?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Dr. Christopher Turk is a surgeon and the best friend of J.D. at Sacred Heart hospital in Scrubs (2001), played by Donald Faison. Their bromance, including the song Guy Love, is the show's heart."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the Nazi in Grey's Anatomy?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Dr. Miranda Bailey is the tough surgical resident nicknamed the Nazi for her standards, who rises to chief of surgery in Grey's Anatomy (2005), played by Chandra Wilson from the first episode onward."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who fixes crises in Scandal?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Olivia Pope is a Washington crisis manager who fixes scandals for the powerful while having an affair with the president in Scandal (2012), played by Kerry Washington, the first Black lead of a network drama in decades."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who teaches criminal law in How to Get Away with Murder?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Annalise Keating is a brilliant, troubled law professor and defense attorney whose students become entangled in murder in How to Get Away with Murder (2014). Viola Davis won an Emmy for the role, a first for a Black woman."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who built the record label in Empire?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Lucious Lyon is a former drug dealer turned hip-hop mogul told he is dying, forcing him to choose an heir to his label in Empire (2015), played by Terrence Howard at the center of the hit drama."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who came home from prison in Empire?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Cookie Lyon is Lucious Lyon's ex-wife, released after 17 years in prison to claim her share of the music empire she helped build in Empire (2015), played by Taraji P. Henson in a star-defining performance."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who raps to herself in the mirror in Insecure?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Issa Dee is a Los Angeles nonprofit worker questioning her job and relationship as she turns 30 in Insecure (2016), played by creator Issa Rae, who built the series from her web series Awkward Black Girl."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who was adopted into the Pearson family in This Is Us?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Randall Pearson is a successful, anxious father adopted as a newborn into the white Pearson family, searching for his birth father in This Is Us (2016). Sterling K. Brown won an Emmy for the role."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the optimistic teacher in Abbott Elementary?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Janine Teagues is a relentlessly optimistic second-grade teacher at an underfunded Philadelphia public school in Abbott Elementary (2021), played by creator Quinta Brunson. The school comedy became a favorite of real teachers everywhere."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who builds a crack empire in Snowfall?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Franklin Saint is a young South Central Los Angeles entrepreneur who builds a crack cocaine empire in the 1980s in Snowfall (2017), played by Damson Idris in the series co-created by John Singleton."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Synclaire James on Living Single?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Synclaire James is the sweet, quirky aspiring actress from Dayton, Ohio, played by Kim Coles on the 1990s sitcom Living Single. Cousin to Khadijah James, she works at Flavor magazine, marries Overton, and gave the show its catchphrase of encouragement, 'Woo woo woo.'"
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Kyle Barker on Living Single?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Kyle Barker is the confident Brooklyn stockbroker played by T.C. Carson on Living Single. Roommate to Overton and sparring partner-turned-romance of Maxine Shaw, Kyle's suits, dreads, and one-liners made him a defining Black sitcom character of the 1990s."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Hilary Banks on The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Hilary Banks is the fashionable, shopping-loving eldest daughter of the Banks family on The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air, played by Karyn Parsons. Her comedy contrasts with her cousin Will's street smarts in the Bel-Air mansion."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Michael Kyle on My Wife and Kids?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Michael Kyle is the wisecracking father on the sitcom My Wife and Kids, played by co-creator Damon Wayans. He teaches his children life lessons through elaborate, funny schemes rather than lectures."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Jay Kyle on My Wife and Kids?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Jay Kyle is the loving, no-nonsense mother on My Wife and Kids, played by Tisha Campbell. She balances her husband Michael's pranks while running the household and pursuing her own ambitions."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Nikki Parker on The Parkers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Nikki Parker is the bold, funny mother who returns to college alongside her daughter Kim on The Parkers, played by Mo'Nique. Her pursuit of Professor Oglevee became the show's running comic storyline."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Kim Parker from Moesha and The Parkers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Kim Parker is the fashion-obsessed, cheerful best friend from Moesha who got her own spin-off, The Parkers, alongside her mother Nikki. Countess Vaughn's comic timing made Kim a favorite of 1990s UPN sitcoms."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Flex Washington on One on One?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Flex Washington is a former basketball player turned sportscaster raising his teenage daughter Breanna alone in Baltimore on the sitcom One on One, played by Flex Alexander. The show centers on a single Black father's learning curve."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Lisa Landry on Sister, Sister?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Lisa Landry is the flamboyant, funny adoptive mother of Tia Landry on Sister, Sister, played by Jack\u00e9e Harry. A seamstress and boutique owner, she brings big energy to the twins' reunited family."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Ray Campbell on Sister, Sister?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Ray Campbell is the widowed limousine-company owner and adoptive father of Tamera Campbell on Sister, Sister, played by Tim Reid. His stiff, proper style comically clashes with Lisa Landry's free spirit."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Mary Jane Paul in Being Mary Jane?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Mary Jane Paul, born Mary Jane Paul and played by Gabrielle Union, is the successful Atlanta cable-news anchor at the center of BET's Being Mary Jane. The series follows her career, family, and search for love, and was a landmark Black women's drama of the 2010s."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Angela Valdes on Power?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Angela Valdes is the federal prosecutor played by Lela Loren on Starz's Power. She hunts the drug kingpin 'Ghost' without knowing he is her former teenage love, James St. Patrick \u2014 the secret that drives the crime drama's first five seasons."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Dre Johnson on Black-ish?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Andre 'Dre' Johnson is the advertising executive father on Black-ish, played by Anthony Anderson. Worried his success distances his kids from their culture, he turns family life into funny lessons on Black identity in America."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Rainbow Johnson on Black-ish?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Rainbow 'Bow' Johnson is the biracial anesthesiologist mother on Black-ish, played by Tracee Ellis Ross, who won a Golden Globe for the role. Bow balances career, five children, and her own identity with warmth and humor."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Earn Marks in Atlanta?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Earnest 'Earn' Marks is the broke Princeton dropout played by series creator Donald Glover on FX's Atlanta. Trying to provide for his daughter, he manages his cousin Alfred's rap career as Paper Boi in a surreal portrait of Black Atlanta life."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Paper Boi in Atlanta?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Alfred 'Paper Boi' Miles is the rising rapper played by Brian Tyree Henry on FX's Atlanta. Managed by his cousin Earn, Alfred's reluctant climb through the music industry \u2014 fame, money, and danger \u2014 anchors the Emmy-winning series created by Donald Glover."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Ghost on the TV show Power?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "James 'Ghost' St. Patrick is a New York nightclub owner secretly running a drug empire on Power, played by Omari Hardwick. Torn between his criminal life and going legitimate, Ghost became one of modern crime television's defining antiheroes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Tariq St. Patrick in the Power universe?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Tariq St. Patrick is Ghost's son, introduced as a child on Power and grown into the lead of the sequel series Power Book II: Ghost, played by Michael Rainey Jr. He reluctantly follows his father's path through the drug world."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Willona Woods on Good Times?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Willona Woods is the Evans family's stylish, sharp-tongued neighbor played by Ja'net DuBois on the 1970s sitcom Good Times. A divorcee who worked in a boutique, she later adopted the abused girl Penny \u2014 one of the show's most remembered storylines."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Beth Pearson on This Is Us?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Beth Pearson is Randall's wife on This Is Us, played by Susan Kelechi Watson. A former dancer and steady family anchor, Beth's humor and honesty made her one of the drama's most beloved characters."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Lawrence on Insecure?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Lawrence Walker is Issa Dee's longtime boyfriend played by Jay Ellis on HBO's Insecure. Unemployed and depressed when the series opens, his breakup with Issa and slow rebuild \u2014 the 'Lawrence Hive' phenomenon \u2014 made him one of the most debated TV boyfriends of the 2010s."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Molly Carter on Insecure?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Molly Carter is Issa's best friend on Insecure, played by Yvonne Orji. A high-achieving corporate lawyer whose personal life is messier than her career, Molly anchors the show's central story about Black female friendship."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Robyn McCall in The Equalizer?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Robyn McCall is a former CIA operative who uses her skills to help people with nowhere else to turn, in the 2021 reboot of The Equalizer, played by Queen Latifah \u2014 the first woman to lead the franchise."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Hondo on S.W.A.T.?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Sergeant Daniel 'Hondo' Harrelson leads a Los Angeles SWAT team on S.W.A.T., played by Shemar Moore. Raised in South Los Angeles, Hondo works to keep trust between his team and the community he came from."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Sergeant Wade Grey on The Rookie?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Sergeant Wade Grey is the watch commander of the Mid-Wilshire police station on The Rookie, played by Richard T. Jones. Stern but fair, he mentors rookie officers including the show's lead, John Nolan."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Nyla Harper on The Rookie?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Nyla Harper is a detective and training officer on The Rookie, played by Mekia Cox. A former undercover officer and mother, she brings hard experience and dry humor to the Mid-Wilshire team from season two onward."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Captain Raymond Holt on Brooklyn Nine-Nine?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Captain Raymond Holt is the deadpan, dignified commanding officer of the 99th precinct on Brooklyn Nine-Nine, played by Andre Braugher. A pioneering Black and gay police captain in the show's story, Holt's dry delivery made him a comedy icon."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Terry Jeffords on Brooklyn Nine-Nine?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Terry Jeffords is the yogurt-loving, muscle-bound sergeant \u2014 later lieutenant \u2014 of the Nine-Nine, played by Terry Crews. Famous for referring to himself in the third person, Terry balances strength with devoted fatherhood."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Winston Bishop on New Girl?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Winston Bishop is the quirky former basketball player and later police officer among the roommates on New Girl, played by Lamorne Morris. His pranks, his cat Ferguson, and his oddball confidence made Winston a late-series fan favorite."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Regine Hunter on Living Single?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Regine Hunter is the fashion-loving, husband-hunting roommate on the 1990s Brooklyn sitcom Living Single, played by Kim Fields. Her designer tastes and comic vanity balanced the show's groundbreaking portrait of young Black professional women."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the Black Panther?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The Black Panther is T'Challa, king and protector of Wakanda, Marvel's fictional African nation, created by Stan Lee and Jack Kirby in 1966. He was the first Black superhero in mainstream American comics and leads with science, strategy, and royal duty."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Shuri, Black Panther's sister?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Shuri is T'Challa's younger sister, a Wakandan princess and one of Marvel's smartest inventors, designing the Black Panther's technology. In the comics she also takes up the Black Panther mantle herself, and Letitia Wright plays her in the films."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Okoye of the Dora Milaje?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Okoye is the general of the Dora Milaje, Wakanda's elite all-women royal guard, and one of T'Challa's most trusted warriors. Danai Gurira's portrayal in the Black Panther films made Okoye a symbol of loyalty and strength."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Killmonger, Black Panther's enemy?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Erik Killmonger, born N'Jadaka, is a Wakandan exile raised in America who challenges T'Challa for the throne, believing Wakanda should arm oppressed people worldwide. He is considered one of Marvel's most compelling villains because his grievance has a point."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Storm of the X-Men?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Storm is Ororo Munroe, a mutant who controls the weather, worshipped as a goddess in Kenya before joining the X-Men in 1975. She became one of Marvel's first major Black heroines and a long-time leader of the X-Men."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Bishop from the X-Men?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Bishop is Lucas Bishop, a mutant police officer from a dystopian future who time-travels to the present-day X-Men. He absorbs energy and fires it back as blasts, and his mission is to prevent his grim future from happening."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Luke Cage?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Luke Cage is a Harlem hero with unbreakable skin and super strength, introduced by Marvel in 1972 as its first Black character to headline his own ongoing series. Framed for a crime, he gains powers in prison and becomes a hero for hire."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Misty Knight?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Misty Knight is a former New York police officer who lost an arm in the line of duty and gained a bionic one, becoming a private investigator and martial artist. She often partners with Colleen Wing as the Daughters of the Dragon."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Blade, the vampire hunter?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Blade is Eric Brooks, a half-human, half-vampire hunter immune to vampire bites, introduced in Marvel's Tomb of Dracula in 1973. Wesley Snipes' Blade film trilogy, beginning in 1998, helped launch the modern era of superhero movies."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is War Machine?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "War Machine is James 'Rhodey' Rhodes, Tony Stark's best friend, a Marine pilot who first appeared in 1979 and later pilots his own heavily armed Iron Man-style armor. Don Cheadle plays Rhodey in the Marvel films."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Sam Wilson, the Falcon?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Sam Wilson, the Falcon, was introduced in 1969 as Marvel's first African-American superhero, Captain America's flying partner from Harlem. In the comics and films he later inherits Captain America's shield, becoming Captain America himself."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Monica Rambeau?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Monica Rambeau is a New Orleans harbor patrol officer turned energy-powered hero who, in 1982, became the second Captain Marvel \u2014 before Carol Danvers took the name. She has led the Avengers and now uses the codename Spectrum."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the Blue Marvel?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The Blue Marvel is Adam Brashear, a Korean War veteran and physicist with immense powers who, in Marvel's retold history, was forced into retirement in the 1960s because America would not accept a Black superman. He returned decades later."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Miles Morales?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Miles Morales is an Afro-Latino teenager from Brooklyn who becomes Spider-Man in Marvel's Ultimate universe, created in 2011. He stars in the Oscar-winning Spider-Verse animated films, voiced by Shameik Moore, with camouflage and venom-blast powers of his own."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Ironheart, Riri Williams?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Ironheart is Riri Williams, a 15-year-old engineering genius from Chicago who builds her own Iron Man-style armor at MIT. Created in 2016, she carries on Tony Stark's legacy and leads Marvel's Champions generation of young heroes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Cloak of Cloak and Dagger?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Cloak is Tyrone Johnson, a runaway teenager whose body became a portal to a darkness dimension, giving him teleportation powers. Paired with Dagger, whose light he needs, the duo debuted in 1982 fighting drugs and street crime."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the Prowler, Aaron Davis?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Aaron Davis, the Prowler, is a burglar in high-tech gear best known today as Miles Morales' uncle, whose death shapes Miles' path as Spider-Man. Donald Glover played Aaron Davis in Spider-Man: Homecoming, and the character looms over the Spider-Verse films."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Spider-Punk?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Spider-Punk is Hobie Brown, a British punk-rock Spider-Man from a world ruled by a tyrant, introduced in Marvel's Spider-Verse comics in 2015. Daniel Kaluuya voiced him in Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse, guitar in hand."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Patriot, Eli Bradley?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Patriot is Eli Bradley, grandson of Isaiah Bradley, the Black Captain America of a secret super-soldier program. A founding Young Avenger from 2005, Eli fights first with attitude and courage, and later with powers from a transfusion of his grandfather's blood."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Isaiah Bradley, the Black Captain America?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Isaiah Bradley was one of 300 Black soldiers experimented on in a secret attempt to recreate the super-soldier serum; he became an underground legend as the Black Captain America. His 2003 comics story was inspired by the real Tuskegee experiments."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Brother Voodoo?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Brother Voodoo is Jericho Drumm, a Haitian houngan \u2014 a Vodou priest \u2014 who became Marvel's master of voodoo magic in 1973, later serving as Sorcerer Supreme. His stories draw on Haitian Vodou religion and Caribbean history."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Night Thrasher?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Night Thrasher is Dwayne Taylor, a wealthy young hero who fights crime on a powered skateboard with martial arts and armor, driven by his parents' murder. He founded Marvel's New Warriors teen team in 1990."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Synch of the X-Men?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Synch is Everett Thomas, a St. Louis teenager whose aura lets him copy the powers of nearby mutants, introduced in Marvel's Generation X in 1994. Long deceased in the comics, he was revived in the Krakoa era as an X-Men leader."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Prodigy, David Alleyne?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Prodigy is David Alleyne, a mutant who automatically absorbs the knowledge and skills of everyone near him, introduced in 2003. A brilliant strategist, he has been a student leader at Xavier's school and a member of the Young Avengers."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Oya of the X-Men?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Oya is Idie Okonkwo, a Nigerian mutant girl who can control temperature \u2014 fire and ice at once \u2014 introduced in 2010 as one of the first new mutants after a long gap in Marvel's story. Storm helps mentor her at Xavier's school."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Gentle of the X-Men?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Gentle is Nezhno Abidemi, a Wakandan mutant student whose strength grows with his body mass, at great physical cost to himself. Raised in Wakanda and trained at Xavier's school, he is one of Marvel's few Wakandan mutants."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is John Stewart, the Green Lantern?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "John Stewart is a former Marine and architect from Detroit chosen as a Green Lantern in 1971, one of DC Comics' first Black superheroes. A generation knows him best as the lead Green Lantern of the Justice League animated series."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Vixen in DC Comics?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Vixen is Mari McCabe, a model from the fictional African nation of Zambesi whose magic Tantu Totem lets her channel the abilities of any animal. Introduced in 1981, she has been a member of the Justice League and the Suicide Squad."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Black Lightning?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Black Lightning is Jefferson Pierce, an Olympic athlete turned high-school principal in a rough Metropolis neighborhood, who uses electrical powers to protect his students. Created in 1977, he was DC's first Black character to headline his own ongoing series."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Lightning, Jennifer Pierce?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Lightning is Jennifer Pierce, younger daughter of Black Lightning, whose light-based electrical powers emerge as a teenager. China Anne McClain played her on The CW's Black Lightning series, alongside her sister Anissa, who fights as Thunder."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Thunder, Anissa Pierce?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Thunder is Anissa Pierce, elder daughter of Black Lightning, who can increase her body density to become nearly invulnerable. Nafessa Williams played her on The CW's Black Lightning \u2014 television's first Black lesbian superhero in a lead role."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Static, Virgil Hawkins?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Static is Virgil Hawkins, a Dakota City teenager who gains electromagnetic powers and builds his own gear, created by Milestone Comics in 1993. His animated series Static Shock made him one of the most beloved Black teen heroes ever."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Icon, Augustus Freeman?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Icon is Augustus Freeman, an alien who crash-landed in the American South in 1839 and took the form of an enslaved Black man, living for over a century as a conservative lawyer \u2014 until a teenager named Rocket pushes him to become a hero."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Rocket, Raquel Ervin?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Rocket is Raquel Ervin, a teenage single mother and aspiring writer from Dakota City who convinces the alien Augustus Freeman to become the hero Icon \u2014 and fights beside him with a gravity-manipulating belt. She narrates Milestone's flagship series."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Hardware in Milestone Comics?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Hardware is Curtis Metcalf, a genius inventor whose employer stole credit for his work, so he built a high-tech suit of armor to expose him. Hardware #1, in 1993, was the very first comic published by Milestone Media."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Mr. Terrific, Michael Holt?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Mr. Terrific is Michael Holt, an Olympic decathlete and one of the smartest men in the DC Universe, whose floating T-Spheres give him high-tech senses and weapons. He first appeared in 1997, inspired by the Golden Age original."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Amanda Waller?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Amanda Waller is the formidable government director who assembles the Suicide Squad \u2014 supervillains sent on missions in exchange for time off their sentences. Introduced in 1986 and played by Viola Davis on screen, 'The Wall' answers to no one."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Cyborg, Victor Stone?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Cyborg is Victor Stone, a star athlete rebuilt with cybernetic body parts by his scientist father after a terrible accident, introduced with the New Teen Titans in 1980. He is a founding screen member of the Justice League and a hero of Detroit."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Bumblebee, DC's bee heroine?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Bumblebee is Karen Beecher, a scientist who built a bee-themed powered suit to help her boyfriend \u2014 then kept it and joined the Teen Titans in the 1970s. She is often counted as DC Comics' first Black female superhero."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Jackson Hyde, the new Aqualad?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Jackson Hyde is a teenager from New Mexico who learns his father is the villain Black Manta and that he has Atlantean water powers, introduced in DC Comics in 2010. A version of him, Kaldur'ahm, leads the team in the Young Justice cartoon."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Nubia, Wonder Woman's sister?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Nubia is Wonder Woman's Black twin sister in DC Comics, introduced in 1973, formed from clay alongside Diana and raised apart from her. In modern stories she becomes Queen of the Amazons, finally given the spotlight after decades in the background."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Batwing, Luke Fox?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Batwing is Luke Fox, son of Batman's technology chief Lucius Fox, an engineer and former MMA fighter who patrols Gotham in a high-tech batsuit. Camrus Johnson played Luke Fox across the Batwoman television series."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is the Signal, Duke Thomas?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The Signal is Duke Thomas, a Gotham teenager with light-manipulating powers whom Batman trains as the city's daytime protector \u2014 the Bat-family's only metahuman for years. He first appeared in 2013 during the Zero Year storyline."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Black Manta, Aquaman's enemy?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Black Manta is David Hyde, a mercenary in a bug-eyed helmet who has hated Aquaman since childhood and devotes his life to destroying him and Atlantis. Introduced in 1967, he is Aquaman's greatest enemy and father of the hero Jackson Hyde."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Steel, John Henry Irons?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Steel is John Henry Irons, an engineer who, believing Superman dead, built a powered suit of armor to carry on his legacy \u2014 his name honoring folk hero John Henry. Shaquille O'Neal played him in the 1997 Steel film."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Natasha Irons?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Natasha Irons is John Henry Irons' niece, a brilliant young engineer who wears her own Steel armor and has also operated as Vaporlock and Starlight in DC Comics. On television's Superman & Lois, her counterpart Natalie Irons crosses from another Earth."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who was Amazing-Man in the Golden Age?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Amazing-Man is Will Everett, an Olympic athlete given matter-absorbing powers, presented by DC Comics in the 1980s as a Black hero of the World War II era \u2014 written as if he had fought alongside the Justice Society all along."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Spawn?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Spawn is Al Simmons, a government assassin murdered and returned from Hell as a hellspawn soldier, created by Todd McFarlane for Image Comics in 1992. Spawn #1 helped launch the creator-owned comics revolution, and the character starred in an acclaimed HBO animated series."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Michonne from The Walking Dead?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Michonne is a katana-wielding survivor who walks the zombie apocalypse with two chained, jawless walkers, introduced in The Walking Dead comic #19 in 2005. Danai Gurira's television portrayal made her one of the franchise's most popular characters."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Josiah X?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Josiah X is Josiah Bradley, son of Isaiah Bradley, the Black Captain America, who grows up hidden from the government and becomes a minister and reluctant hero in Marvel's The Crew in 2003. He carries a version of his father's shield."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Fat Albert?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Fat Albert is the kind-hearted leader of the Junkyard Band in Fat Albert and the Cosby Kids, the 1970s Saturday-morning cartoon created and hosted by Bill Cosby, who also voiced Albert. The show taught life lessons through music and friendship."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Valerie Brown in Josie and the Pussycats?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Valerie Brown is the bassist and songwriter of the all-girl band in Hanna-Barbera's Josie and the Pussycats cartoon from 1970. She is celebrated as one of the first Black female characters to star in a Saturday-morning animated series."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Gerald on Hey Arnold!?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Gerald Johanssen is Arnold's best friend on Nickelodeon's Hey Arnold!, voiced by Jamil Walker Smith. Keeper of the neighborhood's urban legends and Arnold's loyal right hand, Gerald is the cool, confident counterbalance to Arnold's optimism."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Susie Carmichael on Rugrats?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Susie Carmichael is the brave, kind older neighbor on Rugrats, introduced in 1993 and voiced by Cree Summer. Unlike the babies' bully Angelica, Susie stands up for the younger kids and often saves the day."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Jodie Landon on Daria?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Jodie Landon is the intelligent, high-achieving student leader at Lawndale High on MTV's Daria, one of the school's few Black students. Her sharp observations about race and expectations made her a standout of 1990s animation."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Vince LaSalle on Recess?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Vince LaSalle is the athletic star of the gang on Disney's Recess, voiced by Rickey D'Shon Collins. The best athlete at Third Street School, Vince is T.J.'s right hand and the playground's fiercest competitor."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is A.J. on The Fairly OddParents?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "A.J. is Timmy Turner's genius best friend on The Fairly OddParents, a wealthy young inventor with a home laboratory and cloning experiments. Voiced by Gary LeRoi Gray, he balances Chester's goofiness with brains and loyalty."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Libby Folfax on Jimmy Neutron?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Libby Folfax is Cindy Vortex's best friend on The Adventures of Jimmy Neutron, Boy Genius, voiced by Crystal Scales. A music lover with a sharp wit, Libby keeps the gang grounded between Jimmy's runaway inventions."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Wade on Kim Possible?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Wade Load is the 10-year-old tech genius who runs Kim Possible's missions from his bedroom computer, voiced by Tahj Mowry. He builds Kim's gadgets, hacks villain systems, and proves a hero does not need to leave home."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Tucker Foley on Danny Phantom?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Tucker Foley is Danny Phantom's tech-obsessed best friend, voiced by Rickey D'Shon Collins. A self-declared techno-geek and meat enthusiast, Tucker helps Danny track ghosts and covers for him with gadgets and quick thinking."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Numbuh Five on Kids Next Door?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Numbuh Five is Abigail Lincoln, the cool-headed spy and second-in-command of Sector V on Codename: Kids Next Door, voiced by Cree Summer. Always in her red cap, she is the team's calm voice of reason on candy-fueled missions."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Penny Proud?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Penny Proud is the 14-year-old heroine of Disney's The Proud Family, voiced by Kyla Pratt. The 2001 series was a landmark: an animated sitcom built around a Black family, following Penny's school life, friendships, and very loud relatives."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Oscar Proud, Penny's dad?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Oscar Proud is Penny's overprotective father and the founder of Proud Snacks on The Proud Family, voiced by Tommy Davidson. His terrible-tasting snacks and loud schemes make him the show's comic engine."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Fillmore from the Disney cartoon?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Cornelius Fillmore is the star of Disney's Fillmore!, a 1970s-cop-show parody set in a middle school, where Fillmore works the Safety Patrol like a detective squad. Voiced by Orlando Brown, he solves cases from hall passes to bike theft."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Foxxy Love on Drawn Together?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Foxxy Love is a parody of Valerie Brown from Josie and the Pussycats, reimagined for the adult animated reality-show spoof Drawn Together and voiced by Cree Summer. The character is a knowing nod to animation's first Black cartoon band member."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Cleveland Brown on Family Guy?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Cleveland Brown is Peter Griffin's soft-spoken neighbor and friend on Family Guy, introduced in 1999 and originally voiced by Mike Henry. Popular enough to headline his own spin-off, The Cleveland Show, he is known for his slow, gentle delivery."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Donna Tubbs on The Cleveland Show?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Donna Tubbs is Cleveland Brown's wife on The Cleveland Show, voiced by Sanaa Lathan. Cleveland's high-school sweetheart, Donna anchors the blended family with her two children from a previous marriage, Roberta and Rallo."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Roberta Tubbs on The Cleveland Show?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Roberta Tubbs is Donna's teenage daughter and Cleveland's stepdaughter on The Cleveland Show, voiced by Reagan Gomez-Preston. Popular and sharp-tongued, Roberta often clashes with her stepbrother Cleveland Jr. in the blended family comedy."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Mack on Daria?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Michael Jordan, nicknamed Mack, is Jodie Landon's boyfriend and the captain of the Lawndale High football team on Daria. One of the school's few Black students alongside Jodie, Mack shares her dry view of the school's expectations."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Princess Tiana?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Tiana is the heroine of Disney's The Princess and the Frog (2009), a hardworking New Orleans waitress saving to open her own restaurant, voiced by Anika Noni Rose. She is Disney's first Black princess, and her story prizes work and family over wishes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Craig in Craig of the Creek?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Craig Williams is the curious, map-making hero of the Cartoon Network series Craig of the Creek. With his friends Kelsey and J.P., he explores the wild creek near his home, turning every afternoon into an adventure about imagination, friendship, and family."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Jessica, Craig's little sister?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Jessica Williams is Craig's smart, organized little sister in Craig of the Creek and the star of her own spin-off, Jessica's Big Little World. She loves schedules, big words, and proving that little kids can handle big responsibilities all by themselves."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Doc McStuffins?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Dottie 'Doc' McStuffins is a young girl in the Disney Junior series Doc McStuffins who runs a clinic for stuffed animals and toys. Inspired by her doctor mother, she teaches preschoolers about health, kindness, checkups, and not fearing the doctor."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Luz Noceda in The Owl House?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Luz Noceda is the Afro-Dominican teenage hero of Disney's The Owl House. Transported to the magical Boiling Isles, this fantasy-loving human apprentice studies witchcraft under Eda the Owl Lady and learns that being weird is a strength, not a flaw."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Gus in The Owl House?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Augustus 'Gus' Porter is Luz's cheerful friend in The Owl House, a young witch at Hexside School who specializes in illusion magic. Skipped ahead in school for his talent, Gus runs the Human Appreciation Society and dreams of visiting the human world."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Kipo Oak?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Kipo Oak is the optimistic hero of Netflix's Kipo and the Age of Wonderbeasts. Searching a post-apocalyptic surface world of mutant animals for her father, Kipo solves conflicts with empathy, music, and courage, and discovers surprising powers of her own."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Lisa in My Dad the Bounty Hunter?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Lisa Franklin is the confident older sister in Netflix's My Dad the Bounty Hunter. She and her brother Sean stow away on their father's work trip and discover he is an intergalactic bounty hunter, turning a family secret into a space adventure."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Tola in Iw\u00e1j\u00fa?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Tola Martins is the curious young hero of Iw\u00e1j\u00fa, a Disney+ animated series set in a futuristic Lagos, Nigeria. Sheltered by her wealthy family, Tola explores the city's mainland with her friend Kole and a robotic lizard, learning how unequal her world is."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Monde in Supa Team 4?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Monde is one of four teenage superheroines in Netflix's Supa Team 4, an animated series set in Lusaka, Zambia. Recruited by a retired secret agent, Monde and her friends balance school, friendship, and saving their city, in Africa's first Netflix animated series."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Zuri from Hair Love?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Zuri Young is the joyful little girl at the heart of Hair Love, the Oscar-winning animated short about a father learning to style his daughter's natural hair. She returns with her parents Stephen and Angela in the animated family series Young Love."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Lyla in Lyla in the Loop?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Lyla Loops is the seven-year-old star of the PBS Kids series Lyla in the Loop. With her family and her sidekick Stu, Lyla solves everyday problems using computational thinking, creativity, and persistence, showing young viewers how to break big challenges into steps."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Rochelle in Win or Lose?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Rochelle is a teenage catcher on the Pickles softball team in Pixar's streaming series Win or Lose. Hardworking and stressed about money and grades, she secretly takes a job and learns, in her own episode, to ask the people who love her for help."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Carole in Carole & Tuesday?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Carole Stanley is a street musician on Mars in the anime series Carole & Tuesday. An orphan working part-time jobs with her keyboard, she teams up with wealthy runaway Tuesday to write songs in a future where most music is made by computers."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Axel in the anime Lazarus?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Axel Gilberto is the agile, parkour-skilled agent at the center of Lazarus, a 2025 anime series set in 2052. Recruited from prison to a task force hunting a scientist whose miracle drug threatens humanity, Axel leads missions across a stylish, music-filled future."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Joe Gardner in Soul?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Joe Gardner is a middle-school band teacher and jazz pianist in Pixar's Soul, voiced by Jamie Foxx. After an accident sends his soul to the Great Before, Joe races back to his body and learns that a meaningful life is built from everyday moments."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Jabari in Entergalactic?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Jabari is a New York street artist in Entergalactic, the animated special created by and starring Kid Cudi. Hired to turn his character Mr. Rager into comics, Jabari balances a dream career with a growing romance with his neighbor Meadow."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Kat in Wendell & Wild?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Katherine 'Kat' Elliot is the punk-styled teenage hero of the stop-motion film Wendell & Wild. Haunted by guilt over her parents' deaths, Kat discovers she is a hellmaiden who can see demons, and must stop a plot against her town's families."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Asha in Disney's Wish?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Asha is the 17-year-old hero of Disney's Wish, voiced by Ariana DeBose. Living in Rosas, a kingdom where the king hoards everyone's wishes, Asha wishes on a star so powerfully that a living Star answers, and she fights to return her people's hopes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Ethan Clade in Strange World?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Ethan Clade is the teenage son in Disney's Strange World, a farm boy who would rather explore than grow the family crop. On a journey inside his planet with his father and grandfather, Ethan helps three generations of Clade men finally understand each other."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Gabi in Vivo?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Gabi Hern\u00e1ndez is the energetic, purple-haired Florida girl in the animated musical Vivo. When a kinkajou arrives carrying her great-uncle's love song for singer Marta Sandoval, Gabi turns the delivery mission into a road trip about family, grief, and being yourself loudly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Bigger Thomas in Native Son?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Bigger Thomas is the 20-year-old Chicago protagonist of Richard Wright's 1940 novel Native Son. Poor and trapped by racism and fear, Bigger commits crimes that lead to a famous trial, making the novel a landmark protest work studied in schools nationwide."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Janie in Their Eyes Were Watching God?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Janie Crawford is the heroine of Zora Neale Hurston's 1937 novel Their Eyes Were Watching God. Through three marriages in Florida's Eatonville and the Everglades, Janie searches for love and her own voice, in a classic of Black and feminist literature."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Celie in The Color Purple?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Celie Johnson is the heroine of Alice Walker's Pulitzer Prize-winning novel The Color Purple. A poor Georgia woman who endures abuse, Celie finds her voice through letters, friendship with singer Shug Avery, and her own business, in a story of survival and sisterhood."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Pecola Breedlove in The Bluest Eye?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Pecola Breedlove is the young girl at the heart of Toni Morrison's first novel, The Bluest Eye. Living in 1940s Ohio and surrounded by messages that beauty means whiteness, Pecola prays for blue eyes, in a heartbreaking story about race and self-worth."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Sethe in Beloved?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Sethe is the heroine of Toni Morrison's Pulitzer Prize-winning novel Beloved. Born enslaved in Kentucky, she escapes to Ohio, but the memory of slavery, embodied by the ghost of her lost baby, haunts her house in this towering American ghost story."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Milkman Dead in Song of Solomon?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Macon Dead III, nicknamed Milkman, is the hero of Toni Morrison's novel Song of Solomon. A restless young Michigan man, he journeys south tracing his family's hidden history and a rumored bag of gold, and discovers the true treasure is his ancestry."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Sula Peace?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Sula Peace is the fearless, unconventional heroine of Toni Morrison's novel Sula. Returning to her Ohio hometown after ten years away, Sula defies every rule of her community, testing her lifelong friendship with Nel and forcing readers to question good and evil."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is John Grimes in Go Tell It on the Mountain?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "John Grimes is the 14-year-old Harlem hero of James Baldwin's first novel, Go Tell It on the Mountain. Over one long day and night in his stepfather's storefront church, John wrestles with faith, family secrets, and the man he is becoming."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Lutie Johnson in The Street?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Lutie Johnson is the mother at the center of Ann Petry's 1946 novel The Street, the first novel by a Black woman to sell over a million copies. Working as a domestic in Harlem, Lutie fights to give her son a better life."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Ifemelu in Americanah?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Ifemelu is the Nigerian heroine of Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie's novel Americanah. Leaving Nigeria for college in America, she starts a sharp blog about race as a Non-American Black person, while her first love Obinze builds a different life between Nigeria and London."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Kambili in Purple Hibiscus?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Kambili Achike is the quiet 15-year-old narrator of Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie's Purple Hibiscus. Sheltered by her wealthy, strict, and violent father in Nigeria, Kambili discovers laughter, freedom, and her own voice during a visit to her aunt's lively home in Nsukka."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Okonkwo in Things Fall Apart?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Okonkwo is the proud Igbo wrestling champion and farmer at the center of Chinua Achebe's Things Fall Apart, the most widely read African novel ever written. Determined never to resemble his gentle father, Okonkwo watches his Nigerian world change as colonizers arrive."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Starr Carter in The Hate U Give?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Starr Carter is the 16-year-old heroine of Angie Thomas's bestselling novel The Hate U Give. After Starr witnesses a police officer shoot her unarmed friend Khalil, she must decide whether to stay silent or speak, in a defining young adult novel."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Bri in On the Come Up?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Brianna 'Bri' Jackson is the 16-year-old aspiring rapper in Angie Thomas's novel On the Come Up. The daughter of a late underground rap legend, Bri battles in the ring to help her struggling family, then faces fame's costs when a song goes viral."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Z\u00e9lie in Children of Blood and Bone?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Z\u00e9lie Adebola is the heroine of Tomi Adeyemi's West African-inspired fantasy Children of Blood and Bone. In the kingdom of Or\u00efsha, where a ruthless king killed the maji and outlawed magic, fishergirl Z\u00e9lie inherits a chance to bring magic back."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Essun in The Fifth Season?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Essun is the heroine of N. K. Jemisin's Hugo Award-winning novel The Fifth Season. An orogene, a person born able to control earthquakes in a world that fears her kind, Essun crosses a breaking continent searching for her kidnapped daughter as civilization collapses."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Yeine in The Hundred Thousand Kingdoms?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yeine Darr is the heroine of N. K. Jemisin's first novel, The Hundred Thousand Kingdoms. Summoned from her northern homeland to the floating city of Sky, half-mortal Yeine is named an heir to the throne and pulled into deadly games among enslaved gods."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Bree Matthews in Legendborn?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Bree Matthews is the heroine of Tracy Deonn's bestselling novel Legendborn. Grieving her mother, Bree infiltrates a secret society of King Arthur's descendants at a Southern university and discovers her own ancestral Rootcraft magic in this Black Southern fantasy."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Dana in Kindred?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Dana Franklin is the heroine of Octavia Butler's novel Kindred. A young Black writer in 1976 Los Angeles, Dana is repeatedly pulled back in time to a Maryland slave plantation, where she must save the white boy who will become her ancestor."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Lilith in Octavia Butler's Dawn?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Lilith Iyapo is the heroine of Octavia Butler's science fiction novel Dawn. Awakened centuries after nuclear war by the alien Oankali, who saved humanity's survivors, Lilith must lead a small group back to a changed Earth, in a story about difference and survival."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Bud in Bud, Not Buddy?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Bud Caldwell is the 10-year-old hero of Christopher Paul Curtis's Newbery Medal-winning novel Bud, Not Buddy. Orphaned in Depression-era Michigan, Bud runs away from foster homes carrying a suitcase of treasures, searching for a jazz bandleader he believes is his father."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Elijah of Buxton?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Elijah Freeman is the 11-year-old hero of Christopher Paul Curtis's novel Elijah of Buxton. The first child born free in Buxton, Canada, a settlement of people who escaped slavery, Elijah must grow brave fast when a preacher steals his neighbors' freedom money."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who tells the story in The Watsons Go to Birmingham?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Kenny Watson is the young narrator of Christopher Paul Curtis's novel The Watsons Go to Birmingham \u2013 1963. His funny Flint, Michigan family drives south to visit Grandma in Alabama, where their trip meets one of the civil rights movement's darkest days."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Deza Malone, the Mighty Miss Malone?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Deza Malone is the brilliant 12-year-old heroine of Christopher Paul Curtis's novel The Mighty Miss Malone. The smartest girl in her Gary, Indiana classroom, Deza keeps her family's spirits up through the Great Depression as they search for her missing father."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Amari in Copper Sun?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Amari is the 15-year-old heroine of Sharon Draper's novel Copper Sun. Stolen from her Ghanaian village and sold into slavery in South Carolina, Amari endures the Middle Passage and plantation life, holding onto hope in this widely taught historical novel."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Isabel in the novel Chains?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Isabel Finch is the 13-year-old heroine of Laurie Halse Anderson's novel Chains. Enslaved by a cruel Loyalist family in Revolutionary War New York, Isabel spies for the Patriots hoping to earn the freedom she and her little sister Ruth were promised."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Cassie Logan in Roll of Thunder, Hear My Cry?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Cassie Logan is the nine-year-old narrator of Mildred Taylor's Newbery Medal-winning novel Roll of Thunder, Hear My Cry. In 1930s Mississippi, Cassie learns why her family's land matters as they stand against racism, night riders, and pressure to give up both."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Sugar in Jewell Parker Rhodes' novel?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Sugar is the 10-year-old heroine of Jewell Parker Rhodes' novel Sugar. Born into slavery and now working on a Louisiana sugar plantation after emancipation, curious Sugar befriends the owner's son and the new Chinese workers, dreaming of a freer life."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Ghost in Jason Reynolds' novel?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Castle Cranshaw, nicknamed Ghost, is the hero of Jason Reynolds' novel Ghost. A boy who learned to run the night his father attacked his family, Ghost is recruited to a track team, where a good coach helps him outrun his past instead."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Jordan Banks in New Kid?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Jordan Banks is the 12-year-old hero of Jerry Craft's graphic novel New Kid, the first graphic novel to win the Newbery Medal. An artist at heart, Jordan navigates a fancy private school where he is one of the few kids of color."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Tristan Strong?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Tristan Strong is the Chicago seventh grader in Kwame Mbalia's novel Tristan Strong Punches a Hole in the Sky. Sent to Alabama after losing his best friend, Tristan accidentally opens a portal into a world where African American folk heroes and African gods are real."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Peter in The Snowy Day?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Peter is the little boy in Ezra Jack Keats's picture book The Snowy Day, which won the Caldecott Medal in 1963. Waking to a snow-covered city, Peter spends the day making tracks, snowballs, and a snowman, in a classic story of childhood wonder."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Ada Twist?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Ada Twist is the endlessly curious young scientist in Andrea Beaty and David Roberts' picture book Ada Twist, Scientist. Silent until age three, Ada now asks 'Why?' about everything, filling her house with experiments, in a bestselling celebration of girls in science."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Styx Malone?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Styx Malone is the cool, fast-talking teenager in Kekla Magoon's novel The Season of Styx Malone. A foster kid who lands in small-town Indiana for one unforgettable summer, Styx pulls brothers Caleb and Bobby Gene into schemes, trades, and his first real friendship."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Sulwe in Lupita Nyong'o's picture book?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Sulwe is the heroine of Lupita Nyong'o's bestselling picture book Sulwe. Born with skin 'the color of midnight,' darker than her family, Sulwe takes a magical journey with Night and Day that teaches her every shade of dark is beautiful."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Grace in Amazing Grace?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Grace is the imaginative heroine of Mary Hoffman's picture book Amazing Grace. Told she cannot play Peter Pan because she is a girl and Black, Grace proves with a stunning audition that she can be anything she imagines, in a beloved classroom classic."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who flies in Faith Ringgold's Tar Beach?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Cassie Louise Lightfoot is the eight-year-old dreamer of Faith Ringgold's Caldecott Honor picture book Tar Beach. Lying on her Harlem rooftop 'tar beach,' Cassie imagines flying over New York City, claiming its bridges and buildings for her family's future."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is CJ in Last Stop on Market Street?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "CJ is the young boy in Matt de la Pe\u00f1a's Newbery Medal-winning picture book Last Stop on Market Street. Riding the bus across the city with his Nana after church, CJ asks why their neighborhood seems dirty and poor, and Nana answers with wonder."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Anansi the spider?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Anansi is the clever spider trickster of West African Akan storytelling, carried to the Caribbean and the American South by enslaved Africans. In hundreds of tales, retold in many picture books, small Anansi outwits bigger animals with brains instead of strength."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Nyasha in Mufaro's Beautiful Daughters?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Nyasha is the kind younger daughter in John Steptoe's Caldecott Honor picture book Mufaro's Beautiful Daughters, a Zimbabwean Cinderella tale. Gentle with everyone from a hungry boy to a garden snake, Nyasha's goodness, not just beauty, wins her the king's heart."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Barret Wallace in Final Fantasy VII?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Barret Wallace is the tough, big-hearted leader of the eco-rebel group AVALANCHE in Final Fantasy VII. With a gun grafted onto his arm, the single father from a destroyed mining town fights the Shinra company that is draining his planet's life energy."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Lee Everett in The Walking Dead game?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Lee Everett is the hero of Telltale's The Walking Dead adventure game. A former professor being taken to prison when the zombie outbreak begins, Lee finds and protects a little girl named Clementine, and players' choices shape their emotional story."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Clementine in The Walking Dead game?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Clementine is the young heroine of Telltale's The Walking Dead games. Found alone in her treehouse by Lee Everett, Clementine grows across four seasons from a frightened eight-year-old into a brave survivor raising a child of her own in a zombie-ruined world."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Marcus Holloway in Watch Dogs 2?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Marcus Holloway is the playful hacker hero of Watch Dogs 2. Falsely flagged as a criminal by a citywide surveillance system in San Francisco, Marcus joins the hacktivist crew DedSec to expose the corporations watching everyone, using drones, parkour, and humor."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Lincoln Clay in Mafia III?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Lincoln Clay is the Vietnam veteran hero of Mafia III, set in 1968 New Bordeaux, a stand-in for New Orleans. Betrayed and left for dead by the Italian mob that murdered his adoptive family, Lincoln builds his own crew to take the city back."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Bayek in Assassin's Creed Origins?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Bayek of Siwa is the Medjay protector hero of Assassin's Creed Origins, set in ancient Egypt. Grieving his murdered son, Bayek hunts a secret order across pyramids and deserts, and with his wife Aya helps found the brotherhood that becomes the Assassins."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Aveline in Assassin's Creed Liberation?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Aveline de Grandpr\u00e9 is the Assassin hero of Assassin's Creed III: Liberation, set in 1760s New Orleans. The daughter of a French merchant and an enslaved African woman, Aveline fights slavery itself, switching personas between lady, servant, and Assassin to free the enslaved."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Who is Ad\u00e9wal\u00e9 in Assassin's Creed?",
